deploy: publish zombie AI throttle + renderer perf hotfix

Real fix for the runtime stutter many users (incl. RTX 5070 Ti +
i7-14700F rigs) hit even after the asset diet. Diagnosis: the
zombie game was JS-thread-bound, not GPU-bound. Source edits
were made in xrctz/DeadTakeover, built, and deployed here.

Changes in the new bundle (games/zombie/assets/index-WjXO7YF1.js):

1. updateZombies: stop ticking every zombie every frame at
   quality level 0. The round-robin code was already in place
   for quality levels >= 1; just extended to level 0. Each
   zombie now ticks at ~30 Hz instead of 60 Hz, halving the
   single-threaded AI/distance-check/LOS cost. Visually
   identical because dt accumulates correctly across skipped
   frames.

2. Sun shadow camera frustum tightened: far 130 -> 75 (matches
   fog reach) and half-size 42 -> 32. Roughly doubles shadow
   texel density on visible geometry and halves shadow pass
   work for offscreen objects.

3. Default pixelRatio cap: 1.25 -> 1.0 standalone, 0.85 when
   embedded in the hub iframe (the iframe is smaller and you
   don't need 4K-DPI crispness inside it). On a 4K display
   this alone roughly halves fragment shader work.

4. MSAA (antialias) disabled in embedded mode. Standalone keeps
   it. MSAA is one of the most expensive fixed costs on
   integrated/lower-end GPUs and the iframe is small enough
   that aliasing is not visually distracting.

5. Adaptive-quality thresholds tightened so it reacts faster:
   downgrade at >20 ms avg (50 fps) instead of >24 ms (41 fps);
   upgrade at <15 ms (66 fps) instead of <17.5 ms (57 fps).

Deploy notes:
- Only the index.html and the new JS bundle changed in this
  repo. CSS and three.js bundles have identical hashes.
- The fat dist textures from the source repo were NOT copied
  over - the diet'd textures from the previous commit are
  preserved.
- Source changes live in xrctz/DeadTakeover at:
    Zombie Open World Game/src/main.js
  and will be committed there separately.
